unlike_only	two	desire more	P3 C1 A2	wants to get more advantage or possessions than others, as Thrasymachus means it	wants to outdo others in practising a skill, doing more than its correct standard
both	two	desire more	P4 C2 A2	wants to get more advantage or possessions than everyone	wants to outdo everyone in practising a skill, ignoring the craft's standard
just	one
unjust	one
knowing	one
ignorant	one
wise	one
good	one
like_wise	one
like_ignorant	one
# In S1, S39 and S42 "desire more" (and "go beyond") is Thrasymachus's grasping for gain.
# In the craft cases (S17-S29) it means exceeding the correct tuning or prescription.
# S35 says "gain more" but is drawn from the craft cases, so I read it in the craft sense.
# A2 links the craft sense to the just and unjust, so I placed it with the second sense.
# "wise" and "good" may also shift: S3 uses them as Thrasymachus's shrewd and advantageous, while S13 means skilled.
# S3 uses neither claim as listed, so I marked both one.
